# sample-ticker

Demo FDC3 spoke app — market data ticker plant.

Served at **http://localhost:3010** via `npm run dev:sample-ticker`.

## What it does

- Connects to the Desktop Agent over FDC3 2.2 (WebSocket)
- Joins the **Green** user channel on startup
- Periodically broadcasts a mock `fx.rate` context object with a simulated EUR/USD mid price
- Raises **ViewChart** and **ViewQuote** intents when the user clicks on a rate row

## Running

```sh
# From the workspace root
npm run dev:sample-ticker
```

The app proxies `/fdc3-plugin.js` from `packages/fdc3-plugin/fdc3-plugin.js` so no separate build step is needed.

## FDC3 integration points

| Mechanism | Detail |
|---|---|
| Broadcast: fdc3.instrument | Sent on the Green channel every ~2 s |
| Intent: ViewChart | Raised on row click; target: any app handling ViewChart |
| Intent: ViewQuote | Raised on row click; target: any app handling ViewQuote |
| Channel | Green (joined on startup) |
